# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in what you use.
#
# The starter roster runs entirely on SUBSCRIPTION AUTH — no API keys:
#   claude_code agents (planner, scout, reviewer)  -> your Claude Code login.
#      Headless/CI: run `claude setup-token` once and set CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN.
#   codex agents (builder, documenter)             -> your `codex login` (ChatGPT plan).
#
# Dollar cost in the trace is real for claude_code (the CLI reports it) and 0
# for codex (subscription; tokens are still tracked — apply API rates yourself
# if you want a dollar figure).
#
# API keys only matter if you point an agent at the pi backend (coding_agent: pi),
# e.g. to run Gemini: set the provider's key the way ~/.pi/agent/models.json
# names it, and write the model as provider/model-id.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=claude          # claude binary if not on PATH
# CODEX_PATH=codex                 # codex binary if not on PATH
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=         # from `claude setup-token`, for headless runs
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary, only if a pi agent is in the roster
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
